@startuml arp-request-reply
participant "Host A\n192.168.0.101 (aa:aa:aa)" as A
participant "Everyone on segment" as All
participant "Host B\n192.168.0.102 (bb:bb:bb)" as B

== ARP Request (broadcast) ==
A -> All : dst MAC=ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\nop=REQUEST\n"who has 192.168.0.102? tell 192.168.0.101"
note right of All
  Every device on the L2 segment
  receives the broadcast frame.
end note

== ARP Reply (unicast) ==
B -> A : dst MAC=aa:aa:aa\nop=REPLY\nsender=192.168.0.102 (bb:bb:bb)
A -> A : cache 192.168.0.102 -> bb:bb:bb

== Gratuitous ARP (unsolicited) ==
B -> All : op=REQUEST, sender IP = target IP\n"192.168.10.0 is now at ac:5a:fc:b7"
note right of All
  No question was asked - this is a
  self-announcement. Used on host
  boot, IP migration, or failover
  (e.g. MetalLB L2 VIP takeover).
  All neighbors update their cache.
end note
@enduml
